    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376-a1">

                <pb facs="0522" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg434"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Military Department of the Polish
                        National Committee</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wielozieyski</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Military Department <lb/> No. 1140</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-25">25 January,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The President Dmowski duly
                    transmitted us your honored of yesterday’s date as well as the telephonic
                    communication of January 23rd for immediate execution.</p>
                <p>Hereby we take the liberty to inform you that the necessary instructions have
                    been given on 23rd January with regard to sending a telegram to the United
                    States in order to discontinue at once all recruiting for the Polish Army.</p>
                <p>We beg to remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wielozieyski</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
